# Build output. Nothing in this directory is ever committed.
#
# The DLLs here are produced from src/ with CMake, and they belong in a GitHub release as an
# attached archive rather than in the history: a binary in a commit outlives the source it was
# built from, and nobody can tell afterwards which revision produced it.
#
# This file is the only thing in here that git tracks, so the directory survives a clone and says
# what it is for.
#
# To fill it:
#     cmake -S . -B build -A Win32
#     cmake --build build --config Release
#     ctest --test-dir build -C Release
#     copy build\dist\dinput.dll and build\dist\mods\*.dll here, plus dist\engine_fixes.ini and
#     src\tools\ (every standalone script this project ships, not a mod DLL and nothing CMake
#     builds - a .ps1/.bat pair is already its own shipped form - copied in as tools\; lives there
#     in an installed copy too, alongside WMAIN.EXE)

*
!.gitignore

